<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Japanese. The English source is quoted above each entry so a reviewer never has to hold two files
    open at once. Terms are fixed by docs/i18n/ja-glossary.md — アプリ別ルール for a per-app rule,
    連絡先別ルール for a per-contact rule, used everywhere so that one feature has one name, and a
    person, チャット for a chat (never 会話), 次のメッセージから取得 for learning the next message
    (never 学習), 最終一致 for last matched, and 固定のチャット ID for a stable chat id. HiLight, LED
    and ID stay in Latin script.

    Two verbs are kept apart the way the English keeps them apart: 一致 is a rule matching a
    notification, 発動 is the flash it then asks for. A rule matches even when a guard swallowed the
    light, which is the whole point of the card's 最終一致 line.

    The distinction the feature rests on is carried by one pair of notes, built to the same shape so
    they read as two halves of one sentence: チャット ID で一致するため、名前が変わっても一致し続けます
    against 名前で一致するため、名前を変更すると一致しなくなることがあります.

    Register: polite-neutral です・ます for captions; labels, buttons, badges and pills are noun
    phrases with no full stop, and questions asked in a title end in ますか with no punctuation, as in
    strings_setup.xml.

    Length: ButtonLabel is single line with no wrapping, so the two buttons sharing a row inside the
    capture card are これを使う and もう一度待つ rather than fuller renderings. The relative stamps take
    the compact no-space form the duration resources use (%1$d分前), while prose keeps the space
    (2 つの方法).
-->
<resources>

    <!-- The screen itself -->
    <!-- "Per-app rules" -->
    <string name="rules_section_title">アプリ別ルール</string>
    <!-- "Keep every light rule for an app together, then add as many specific notification rules as you need." -->
    <string name="rules_intro_apps">アプリごとにすべてのライト設定をまとめ、必要なだけ個別の通知ルールを追加できます。</string>
    <!-- "Contacts and chats keep their existing matching, and text rules can match any word or phrase Android exposes." -->
    <string name="rules_intro_messaging">連絡先やチャットの既存の判定はそのまま使え、Android が公開する単語やフレーズでも通知を判定できます。</string>
    <!-- "Add app" -->
    <string name="rules_add_app">アプリを追加</string>
    <string name="rules_add_short">ルール</string>
    <string name="rules_collapse">ルールを折りたたむ</string>
    <string name="rules_expand">ルールを展開</string>
    <plurals name="rules_group_status">
        <item quantity="other">%1$d 件のルール · %2$d 件有効</item>
    </plurals>

    <!-- Compact rows: what the rule matches, what the LEDs do, and when it last matched. -->

